''आङ्ग्लभाषान्तरम् (English Translation)''

''Commentary Title: Mandopakāriṇī (on Verse 32)''

* ''Primary Historical Meaning:'' Having burnt the lac house to ashes, emerging from the subterranean tunnel, and carrying his brothers led by Yudhishthira on his shoulders like embodied virtues, Bhima—who became the enemy of the demon Hidimba—beheld Lord Vedavyasa, who appeared to facilitate the marriage of Hidimbi to Bhima.

* ''First Analogy (The Secret Agent/Spy):'' Just as a clever spy, using strategic means, burns down an enemy's city, emerges unharmed without being broken by foes, protects his companions, and reaches his sovereign master.

* ''Second Analogy (The Enlightened Yogi):'' Just as an accomplished Yogi, through the perfection of //samadhi// and //pranayama//, dissolves the physical body in the internal fire, departs through the //Brahma-nadi// without suffering physical rupture (//adari-bhāva*), and carrying the merit acquired for liberation, attains Supreme Lord Narayana.